PART 1 CONCLUSION (complete and honest)
==============================================================================
The complete non-reducible squared-trace locus of tr(B)^2=tr(Abb)^2
has TWO components, not one: X_{-2,3} exactly (component 0 of the
C_plus branch), and a second, distinct irreducible component (from
the C_minus branch) whose exact geometric identity (which slope, if
any specific one) is NOT established here -- an identification
attempt was tried and found inconclusive, and is reported as such
rather than asserted. Both reducible components (one per branch) are
confirmed genuinely reducible via the exact Fricke criterion.

This means the STRONGER claim 'the complete exact locus equals
X_{-2,3} alone' is NOT what was found -- report two components. The
atlas's original empirical claim (unique among the 13 CHECKED points)
is untouched by this, since it was never a claim about the full
algebraic locus, only about those 13 specific fillings.

