==============================================================================
PART 2 CONCLUSION
==============================================================================
Since the identity g B g^-1 (Abb)^-1 = 1 (g=BaBA) holds as an exact
polynomial consequence at EVERY representation on the (-2,3) filled
variety, it holds in particular at the discrete-faithful geometric
representation. That representation is FAITHFUL (a standard fact
for the holonomy of a complete finite-volume hyperbolic structure),
so an exact matrix identity there already proves the abstract group
identity

   (BaBA) * B * (BaBA)^-1 = (Abb)^-1   in pi_1(m003(-2,3)),

i.e. B and Abb are CONJUGATE (via the inverse) in the filled group
itself -- not merely equal in trace, and not merely true at one
representation. This is the strong group-theoretic mechanism: since
conjugate elements automatically have equal trace under ANY
representation of the group, tr(B)=tr(Abb) for the (-2,3)-filled
group follows for every SL2(C) representation whatsoever, not just
the ones on the character variety already checked.

